Backport of PR #823 onto the pinned PR #822 source.
Origin: https://github.com/Zackriya-Solutions/meetily/pull/823
Commit: 616128f1f6788e9453127714ecbf3a9add5706b0
Only hunk context is adjusted for the older ring buffer, logging, and saver.

From 616128f1f6788e9453127714ecbf3a9add5706b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dreamkeeper <dkvasnikov@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:21:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(recording): optionally save mic and system audio as
 separate channels

Adds an opt-in "Save Separate Channels" recording setting (off by default).
When enabled, the pipeline also writes audio_stereo.mp4 next to audio.mp4:
left channel = microphone, right channel = system audio, built from the same
aligned mixer windows as the mixed file. metadata.json records the file as
audio_file_stereo with audio_file_stereo_channels ["microphone", "system"].
The mixed audio.mp4, live transcription and retranscription are unchanged.

Also fixes mixer alignment: a window was extracted as soon as either stream
had enough samples, so a stream whose packet was still in flight got
zero-padded mid-signal and its samples slid into the next window (short
dropouts in the mix, drifting mic/system offset). Windows are now taken when
both streams can fill them, or when one stream is 300 ms ahead (the other has
stalled, e.g. WASAPI loopback with nothing playing). Samples left in the ring
buffer at stop are now written instead of dropped.

Refs #241

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
